让我想起了西装仓库那一集，德怀特和吉姆说他们以前假装成兄弟打电话推销，

919
00:39:21.750 --> 00:39:24.510
and Dwight says they were Jim and Dwight Schruppert.
然后德怀特说他们叫吉姆和德怀特·施鲁珀特。

920
00:39:24.850 --> 00:39:25.670
Oh yeah.
哦，对。

921
00:39:26.030 --> 00:39:26.770
Isn't that cute?
那不是很可爱吗？

922
00:39:26.970 --> 00:39:28.150
That's super cute.
超级可爱。

923
00:39:28.290 --> 00:39:28.830
I know.
我知道。

924
00:39:28.930 --> 00:39:30.530
I love those scenes too.
我也很喜欢那些场景。

925
00:39:30.910 --> 00:39:35.250
Well, lady, I just remember your big idea when we were going to be mom detectives
得了吧，女士，我只记得你那个绝妙的主意，当时我们打算当妈妈侦探，

926
00:39:35.250 --> 00:39:38.250
to figure out what was going on in the windowless building.
去搞清楚那栋没有窗户的建筑里在搞什么鬼。

927
00:39:38.430 --> 00:39:39.390
Do you remember it?
你还记得吗？

928
00:39:39.490 --> 00:39:40.570
Because it was very funny.
因为真的太搞笑了。

929
00:39:41.150 --> 00:39:42.210
No, I don't.
不，我不记得了。

930
00:39:42.330 --> 00:39:48.130
You said that the way we get into the building is that we should deliver them
你说我们混进那栋楼的方法应该是给他们送点东西，

931
00:39:48.130 --> 00:39:51.270
like a fruit basket or some flowers.
比如一篮水果或者一些花。

932
00:39:52.430 --> 00:39:54.730
And you were like, I was like, what?
然后你说，我说，什么？

933
00:39:55.210 --> 00:39:57.630
We're going to take a fruit basket in?
我们要送一篮水果进去？

934
00:39:57.810 --> 00:39:59.490
I'm like, no, we're just going to walk in.
我说，不用，我们直接走进去就行。

935
00:39:59.590 --> 00:40:00.370
Just walk in.
直接走进去。

936
00:40:00.470 --> 00:40:00.970
Let's just go.
我们走吧。

937
00:40:01.090 --> 00:40:02.730
And you're like, no, we need a reason.
而你说，不行，我们需要一个理由。

938
00:40:02.930 --> 00:40:04.510
We need a thing.
我们需要个借口。

939
00:40:04.590 --> 00:40:05.470
We need a cover.
我们需要个掩护。

940
00:40:05.690 --> 00:40:07.030
And then you walked in.
然后你走了进去。

941
00:40:07.130 --> 00:40:09.890
We walked in together and you were like, hey.
我们一起走了进去，然后你来了句，嘿。

942
00:40:10.090 --> 00:40:11.510
And then you went blank.
接着你就大脑一片空白了。

943
00:40:11.690 --> 00:40:15.050
There was like this weird moment and this guy is just looking at us.
当时气氛有点诡异，那家伙就一直看着我们。

944
00:40:15.170 --> 00:40:18.110
And then finally you're like, we're just wondering, what is this place?
然后你终于憋出一句，我们就是想知道，这到底是什么地方？

945
00:40:18.170 --> 00:40:19.550
You just asked him.
你直接就问他了。

946
00:40:19.550 --> 00:40:23.820
I was like, let's not beat around the bush.
当时我想的是，咱们别拐弯抹角了。

947
00:40:24.040 --> 00:40:28.860
There were some clues as we walked up the ramp to get inside.
当我们走上斜坡进去的时候，其实有一些线索的。

948
00:40:28.940 --> 00:40:31.980
There were some elderly people having some sunshine.
有一些老人在那里晒太阳。

949
00:40:32.300 --> 00:40:32.560
Yeah.
对。

950
00:40:32.980 --> 00:40:33.920
But still.
但还是觉得奇怪。

951
00:40:34.160 --> 00:40:34.440
Yeah.
是啊。

952
00:40:34.980 --> 00:40:35.460
Yeah.
对。

953
00:40:35.960 --> 00:40:37.060
It was very clear.
非常清楚。

954
00:40:37.340 --> 00:40:38.700
People there were of a certain age.
那里的人都在一定的年纪。

955
00:40:39.100 --> 00:40:39.540
Yeah.
对。

956
00:40:39.820 --> 00:40:39.960
Yeah.
是啊。

957
00:40:40.380 --> 00:40:41.700
Why are you dancing around it?
你为什么拐弯抹角的？

958
00:40:41.840 --> 00:40:42.480
I don't know.
我不知道。

959
00:40:42.640 --> 00:40:44.200
The thing I found most interesting though.
不过我发现最有趣的一点是。

960
00:40:44.380 --> 00:40:44.580
What?
什么？

961
00:40:44.580 --> 00:40:46.320
Is that he said, we're a senior center.
就是他说，我们是个老年活动中心。

962
00:40:46.920 --> 00:40:48.440
And I was like, yeah, ding, ding, ding.
然后我就想，对，答对了，就是这样。

963
00:40:48.620 --> 00:40:51.680
And he goes, but we also rented out for weddings.
接着他说，但我们也会把场地租出去办婚礼。

964
00:40:52.360 --> 00:40:53.380
No, he did not.
不，他没这么说吧。

965
00:40:53.460 --> 00:40:53.720
Yes.
说了。

966
00:40:53.820 --> 00:40:54.320
Is that true?
真的吗？

967
00:40:54.500 --> 00:40:54.940
That back room.
后面那个房间。

968
00:40:55.240 --> 00:40:57.740
That room where they were like playing cards and stuff.
就是他们打牌什么的那个房间。

969
00:40:57.820 --> 00:40:59.180
You can also rent that out.
那个也可以租出去。

970
00:41:00.860 --> 00:41:01.820
I missed that.
我怎么漏掉了这个。

971
00:41:01.900 --> 00:41:02.200
Oh, yeah.
哦，对。

972
00:41:02.340 --> 00:41:03.200
How did I miss that?
我怎么会错过这个？

973
00:41:03.200 --> 00:41:03.740
I don't know.
我不知道。

974
00:41:03.740 --> 00:41:06.340
So you were jotting something down on your notepad that you had.
所以你刚才在你的记事本上写写画画。

975
00:41:06.460 --> 00:41:11.760
But he said you can also, you know, sometimes we do like events, you know, like wedding receptions,
但他说了你也可以，你知道的，有时我们也会办活动，你知道的，比如婚宴之类的，

976
00:41:11.880 --> 00:41:12.420
things like that.
诸如此类的事情。

977
00:41:13.760 --> 00:41:15.020
That's fascinating to me.
这让我觉得很有意思。

978
00:41:15.020 --> 00:41:16.700
I feel like I need to go back.
我觉得我得回去一趟。

979
00:41:17.220 --> 00:41:17.620
No.
不行。

980
00:41:17.620 --> 00:41:20.400
Also, by the way, it wasn't a live-in facility.
另外，顺便说一句，那不是一家住养机构。

981
00:41:20.660 --> 00:41:20.820
No.
不是。

982
00:41:20.820 --> 00:41:21.460
So that makes sense.
所以这就说得通了。

983
00:41:21.660 --> 00:41:26.420
During the day, it was just a daytime facility for elderly people to go to.
白天的时候，它只是老年人白天去的一个场所。

984
00:41:26.600 --> 00:41:27.120
A senior center.
一个老年活动中心。

985
00:41:27.320 --> 00:41:27.420
Right.
对。

986
00:41:27.420 --> 00:41:30.380
Where they can go play cards or bridge or they'll have someone come in like.
他们可以在那里打牌或打桥牌，或者会有人来做客。

987
00:41:30.980 --> 00:41:33.260
But there's nurses and physical therapy there too.
但那里也有护士和物理治疗。

988
00:41:33.260 --> 00:41:33.680
Yes.
对。

989
00:41:33.980 --> 00:41:34.320
Right.
没错。

990
00:41:34.660 --> 00:41:36.660
But that room where they play cards and stuff.
但他们打牌什么的那个房间。

991
00:41:36.760 --> 00:41:37.200
At night.
到了晚上。

992
00:41:37.360 --> 00:41:39.820
You could also have your, you know.
你也可以用来办，你知道的。

993
00:41:40.160 --> 00:41:41.320
What a business model.
多棒的商业模式啊。

994
00:41:41.320 --> 00:41:41.940
Wedding reception.
婚宴。

995
00:41:42.600 --> 00:41:42.760
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

996
00:41:42.900 --> 00:41:43.120
Hmm.
嗯。

997
00:41:43.520 --> 00:41:44.160
All right.
好吧。

998
00:41:44.300 --> 00:41:50.800
Well, now they're inside of the mattress store and they're talking to Cindy, the mattress store employee,
嗯，现在他们走进了床垫店，正和床垫店的员工辛迪交谈，

999
00:41:51.260 --> 00:41:53.200
and they ask about a particular mattress.
他们询问某款特定的床垫。

1000
00:41:53.200 --> 00:41:55.420
And she says, oh, this one's great.
然后她说，哦，这款真的很棒。

1001
00:41:55.640 --> 00:41:56.740
It's $1,900.
要1900美元。

1002
00:41:57.420 --> 00:41:59.680
And Ned is like, well, you know what?
然后内德就说，你知道吗？

1003
00:42:00.100 --> 00:42:02.860
You guys have like a price match guarantee, right?
你们店里有价格匹配保证，对吧？

1004
00:42:02.860 --> 00:42:07.520
I was down at this other mattress store and I saw this mattress for $14.50.
我去过另一家床垫店，看到这款床垫只卖14.50美元。

1005
00:42:07.520 --> 00:42:09.040
Would you honor that price?
你们会按这个价格卖给我吗？

1006
00:42:09.280 --> 00:42:15.060
And she's like, oh, no, you didn't see this mattress because this is exclusive to our store.
她就说，哦，不，你绝对没看到这款床垫，因为这是我们店独家发售的。

1007
00:42:15.280 --> 00:42:15.660
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1008
00:42:15.660 --> 00:42:16.740
And he's like, really?
然后他问，真的吗？

1009
00:42:16.840 --> 00:42:18.040
It looks like the same mattress.
这看起来完全是一样的床垫啊。

1010
00:42:18.320 --> 00:42:19.020
Could you go check?
你能去查一下吗？

1011
00:42:19.240 --> 00:42:20.560
This is part of the scam.
这就是骗局的一部分。

1012
00:42:20.820 --> 00:42:21.220
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1013
00:42:21.900 --> 00:42:22.560
Guess what?
你猜怎么着？

1014
00:42:22.780 --> 00:42:28.120
This whole storyline is based on a true story from Greg Daniels' life.
整个故事线都是根据格雷格·丹尼尔斯生活中的真实事件改编的。

1015
00:42:28.980 --> 00:42:37.460
Greg Daniels was trying to find a mattress that he loved and he was trying to buy it again because he loved it, but he needed a new one.
格雷格·丹尼尔斯当时想找一张他很喜欢的床垫，因为太喜欢了所以想再买一个同样的，但他需要买个新的。

1016
00:42:37.460 --> 00:42:39.960
So, he couldn't find it.
结果，他根本找不到。

1017
00:42:40.180 --> 00:42:42.540
This is when he uncovered the truth.
就在这时，他揭开了真相。

1018
00:42:42.740 --> 00:42:47.100
The truth, which is that mattress stores do this.
真相就是，床垫店都是这么干的。

1019
00:42:47.380 --> 00:42:54.220
They have exclusive names for the exact same mattresses so that you can't compare prices.
他们给完全一模一样的床垫起不同的独家名字，这样你就没法比价了。

1020
00:42:54.220 --> 00:42:56.100
I looked it up, lady.
大姐，我都查过了。

1021
00:42:56.520 --> 00:43:07.120
There are a gazillion, gazillion Reddit threads and websites dedicated to decoding all of the names for all these mattresses that are actually the same mattress.
网上有无数个、成千上万个红迪网帖子和网站，专门用来破解这些实际上是同一款床垫的各种名字。

1022
00:43:07.420 --> 00:43:07.940
Wow.
哇。

1023
00:43:08.120 --> 00:43:08.580
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1024
00:43:09.080 --> 00:43:09.480
Yeah.
是啊。

1025
00:43:09.660 --> 00:43:17.220
And I feel like it made its way into this episode as Greg's little way of exposing this to the world.
我觉得这个情节出现在这集里，成了格雷格向全世界揭露这件事的小小方式。

1026
00:43:17.220 --> 00:43:17.940
He's like, I got you.
他就像是在说，我抓到你们了。

1027
00:43:18.040 --> 00:43:18.200
Yeah.
是啊。

1028
00:43:18.280 --> 00:43:19.040
I got your number.
我摸清你们的底细了。

1029
00:43:19.040 --> 00:43:19.540
It was expose.
这是一次曝光。

1030
00:43:20.160 --> 00:43:20.440
Yeah.
是啊。

1031
00:43:21.260 --> 00:43:28.220
Well, I did ask Mary, who plays Cindy, if they filmed in a real mattress store or if that was a set they built.
我问过饰演辛迪的玛丽，他们是在真正的床垫店拍的，还是搭建的布景。

1032
00:43:28.360 --> 00:43:29.840
And here's what she said.
她是这么回答的。

1033
00:43:30.400 --> 00:43:32.640
She said, yep, it was a real mattress store.
她说，没错，那是家真正的床垫店。

1034
00:43:32.780 --> 00:43:34.980
So, at lunch, I just went ahead and laid down.
所以午休时，我就直接躺上午休了。

1035
00:43:36.220 --> 00:43:36.660
Wow.
哇。

1036
00:43:36.900 --> 00:43:37.700
That's amazing.
太棒了。

1037
00:43:37.940 --> 00:43:40.920
She also said that everyone she met that day was so lovely.
她还说，那天遇到的每个人都非常可爱。

1038
00:43:41.160 --> 00:43:45.700
There was no ego, no tension, just really funny pros on and off screen.
没有勾心斗角，没有紧张气氛，无论台前幕后都是非常搞笑的专业人士。

1039
00:43:45.980 --> 00:43:48.440
She also said a crew can really make the set feel cozy.
她还说，剧组真的能让片场感觉像家一样温馨。

1040
00:43:48.440 --> 00:43:53.100
And for a guest star who's in for one day, it's so lovely to be greeted by everyone so warmly.
对于只客串一天的演员来说，受到大家如此热烈的欢迎真是太美妙了。

1041
00:43:53.240 --> 00:43:55.800
I felt like family, even though it was just for the day.
我觉得自己就像是一家人，尽管只呆了一天。

1042
00:43:56.080 --> 00:44:00.440
And then she had one other thing I want to share about shooting these big scenes.
关于拍摄这些大场面，她还有一件事我想分享一下。

1043
00:44:00.680 --> 00:44:03.160
There are big scenes in this huge room, right?
在这个巨大的房间里有很多大场面，对吧？

1044
00:44:03.640 --> 00:44:07.540
She said, I had never shot a documentary-style TV show.
她说，我以前从来没拍过纪录片风格的电视剧。

1045
00:44:07.780 --> 00:44:11.400
So, it actually didn't dawn on me when we were filming for real.
所以正式拍摄的时候，我其实根本没意识到。

1046
00:44:12.100 --> 00:44:13.820
She didn't know where the cameras were.
她不知道摄像机在哪里。

1047
00:44:13.960 --> 00:44:16.920
She didn't know they were filming until they wrapped her first scene.
直到她的第一场戏拍完，她才知道原来一直在拍。

1048
00:44:17.500 --> 00:44:19.880
She said, I'm so used to cameras being really invasive.
她说，我太习惯那种极具侵入性的摄像机了。

1049
00:44:20.260 --> 00:44:23.640
You know, they're right there where you can see them with cords and lights all around.
你知道的，它们就在你能看到的地方，周围全是电线和灯光。

1050
00:44:23.920 --> 00:44:28.600
And she said, I didn't know where the cameras were until one of the grips started,
她说，直到其中一个场务开始动，我才知道摄像机在哪儿

1051
00:44:28.860 --> 00:44:32.800
a la Dear Evan Hansen style, waving through the window, way over here.
就像《致埃文·汉森》那样，在窗前挥手，就在这边。

1052
00:44:33.020 --> 00:44:33.860
We're over here.
我们在这边。

1053
00:44:34.880 --> 00:44:35.280
Wow.
哇。

1054
00:44:35.600 --> 00:44:35.760
Yeah.
是啊。

1055
00:44:35.960 --> 00:44:37.160
Because she was like, are we filming?
因为她当时问，我们在拍吗？

1056
00:44:37.440 --> 00:44:38.180
Like, where are the cameras?
就像是，摄像机在哪？

1057
00:44:38.340 --> 00:44:39.920
That's how far away the cameras were.
摄像机当时离得就是那么远。

1058
00:44:40.040 --> 00:44:41.540
And that's what you were talking about.
而这就是你刚才说的。

1059
00:44:41.540 --> 00:44:43.120
Yeah, the super spy shots.
对，就是超远距离偷拍那种感觉。

1060
00:44:43.320 --> 00:44:49.460
Yeah, that the director was creating this very cool vibe on the set that you didn't even see the cameras.
对，导演在片场营造了一种非常酷的氛围，你甚至都看不到摄像机。

1061
00:44:49.680 --> 00:44:49.980
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1062
00:44:50.420 --> 00:44:52.280
Well, now we're going to go into this meeting.
好了，现在我们要进入这场会议了。

1063
00:44:52.860 --> 00:44:54.200
Marv is running this meeting.
马夫在主持这场会议。

1064
00:44:54.200 --> 00:44:56.760
It's with Esmeralda, Ken, and Oscar.
与会者有埃斯梅拉达、肯和奥斯卡。

1065
00:44:56.960 --> 00:44:59.140
And there's supposed to be a fourth person there.
本来应该还有第四个人出席的。

1066
00:44:59.680 --> 00:45:01.060
Ned, he's missing.
内德，他失踪了。

1067
00:45:01.200 --> 00:45:01.780
He's missing.
他不见了。

1068
00:45:02.140 --> 00:45:05.180
I called these scenes big boardroom budget meeting.
我把这些场景叫做大型董事会预算会议。

1069
00:45:05.180 --> 00:45:08.620
Oh, Ken calls it bi-weekly budget meeting.
哦，肯管它叫双周预算会议。

1070
00:45:10.620 --> 00:45:12.100
But I like your name, too.
不过我也挺喜欢你起的名字。

1071
00:45:12.620 --> 00:45:14.060
Big boardroom budget meeting.
大型董事会预算会议。

1072
00:45:15.320 --> 00:45:19.280
Well, we're just not in this big boardroom very often, and it looks prestigious.
好吧，我们平时不常进这么大的董事会会议室，它看起来挺高级的。

1073
00:45:19.720 --> 00:45:21.720
It looks like a place where important things happen.
看起来就像是个会发生重要事情的地方。

1074
00:45:21.980 --> 00:45:23.420
Yeah, this is on another floor.
对，这在另一层楼。

1075
00:45:23.620 --> 00:45:25.220
This is on the executive level.
这是行政楼层。

1076
00:45:25.460 --> 00:45:26.880
This is Marv's world.
这是马夫的地盘。

1077
00:45:27.080 --> 00:45:27.540
That's right.
没错。

1078
00:45:28.020 --> 00:45:31.740
Well, Esmeralda is just going to continue to throw Ned under the bus.
好吧，埃斯梅拉达接下来要继续把内德当替罪羊甩锅了。

1079
00:45:31.900 --> 00:45:34.060
Yeah, she's super sabotagey in this scene.
对，她在这一场里简直是个超级破坏王。

1080
00:45:34.060 --> 00:45:35.820
She's making him seem incompetent.
她在把他说得像个无能的人一样。

1081
00:45:36.020 --> 00:45:37.880
Like, she says, I told him about the meeting.
比如她说，我告诉过他开会的事了。

1082
00:45:38.000 --> 00:45:44.080
But what she did was she put a little sticky note that says, M-O-B-M-I-A-B.
但她实际做的是，留了一张写着“M-O-B-M-I-A-B”的小便签。

1083
00:45:44.380 --> 00:45:45.880
On his computer, yes.
贴在他的电脑上，对。

1084
00:45:46.080 --> 00:45:49.780
Which I guess means Marv's office budget meeting in a bit.
我猜这大概意思是“马夫的办公室预算会议一会儿开”。

1085
00:45:50.360 --> 00:45:52.600
And, you know, of course he didn't know what that was.
而且，你知道的，他当然不知道那是什么意思。

1086
00:45:52.720 --> 00:45:53.000
Right.
对。

1087
00:45:53.160 --> 00:45:55.620
But she's going to tell Marv, oh, I told him about the meeting.
但她会跟马夫说，哦，我告诉过他开会的事了。

1088
00:45:55.740 --> 00:45:55.880
Yeah.
是啊。

1089
00:45:55.960 --> 00:45:56.780
I left him a note.
我给他留了便条。

1090
00:45:56.940 --> 00:45:59.900
She doesn't tell him she left a note saying, mob meab.
她可没告诉马夫她留的便条上写的是一堆缩写代号。

1091
00:46:01.360 --> 00:46:04.680
I love that you took on pronouncing it.
我太喜欢你把它读出来了。

1092
00:46:05.100 --> 00:46:12.060
Now we're back at Nicole and Detrick's desks, and they're doing some would you rather questions
现在我们回到了妮可和迪特里克的办公桌旁，他们正在玩“你更愿意”这种问题游戏

1093
00:46:12.060 --> 00:46:14.120
to try to learn about one another.
来试图了解彼此。

1094
00:46:14.860 --> 00:46:20.960
Yeah, they say, would you rather be able to speak to animals or speak any human language
对，他们说，你更愿意能够跟动物对话，还是说任何你想说的

1095
00:46:20.960 --> 00:46:23.080
ever that you ever wanted to speak?
人类语言？

1096
00:46:23.260 --> 00:46:24.960
I want us to answer this question.
我想让我们俩也回答这个问题。

1097
00:46:25.180 --> 00:46:25.960
I have it too.
我也有同感。

1098
00:46:25.960 --> 00:46:28.100
I said, Jenna, what do you pick?
我说，珍娜，你选哪个？

1099
00:46:28.540 --> 00:46:29.980
This is really hard for me.
这对真的我来说太难了。

1100
00:46:30.060 --> 00:46:30.600
I don't know.
我不知道。

1101
00:46:31.420 --> 00:46:33.020
Because they're both really good.
因为它们两个真的都很棒。

1102
00:46:33.200 --> 00:46:35.620
This is a very good would you rather.
这是一个非常棒的“你更愿意”问题。

1103
00:46:35.860 --> 00:46:38.340
Is this the best would you rather question?
这会是史上最好的“你更愿意”问题吗？

1104
00:46:39.520 --> 00:46:40.420
Like, is it the best?
比如说，它是最好的吗？

1105
00:46:40.420 --> 00:46:41.940
In the history of would you rathers?
在“你更愿意”的历史上？

1106
00:46:42.020 --> 00:46:42.500
Maybe.
也许吧。

1107
00:46:43.020 --> 00:46:43.500
Maybe.
