非常像埃德·格里姆利。

1265
00:53:25.000 --> 00:53:27.260
But this was really exciting to me.
但这对我来说真的很激动人心。

1266
00:53:27.540 --> 00:53:30.220
I was rooting for them to have a good article.
我真希望他们能写出一篇好报道。

1267
00:53:30.460 --> 00:53:33.260
You know, this is our third episode in the series now,
你知道，这是我们系列的第三集了，

1268
00:53:33.260 --> 00:53:36.760
and this is kind of the first win for the paper.
这可以说是报社的第一次胜利。

1269
00:53:37.060 --> 00:53:37.320
Yeah.
对。

1270
00:53:37.560 --> 00:53:38.500
Don't you feel like that?
你不觉得吗？

1271
00:53:38.500 --> 00:53:39.160
Yeah, for sure.
是的，当然。

1272
00:53:39.160 --> 00:53:40.440
I was happy for them, too.
我也为他们感到高兴。

1273
00:53:40.780 --> 00:53:45.940
And of course, when Cindy does eventually come back, they confront her.
当然，当辛迪最终回来时，他们当面质问她。

1274
00:53:46.220 --> 00:53:50.600
They say, we're from the truth teller doing a report on consumer protection.
他们说，我们是“实话实说”栏目的，正在做一份关于消费者保护的报道。

1275
00:53:50.980 --> 00:53:53.260
And she's like, I knew your mother wasn't sick.
然后她说，我就知道你妈没生病。

1276
00:53:53.540 --> 00:53:55.880
And then basically, she's like, I'm not going to say anything.
然后基本上，她说，我什么都不会说。

1277
00:53:55.880 --> 00:53:56.840
You have no proof.
你们没有证据。

1278
00:53:57.000 --> 00:53:58.720
And then they point to the cameras.
接着他们指向摄像机。

1279
00:53:59.060 --> 00:53:59.400
Yes.
是的。

1280
00:53:59.780 --> 00:54:01.980
They say, actually, we do have proof.
他们说，其实，我们有证据。

1281
00:54:02.260 --> 00:54:03.560
Here is one camera.
这是一个摄像机。

1282
00:54:03.780 --> 00:54:04.520
Here is another camera.
这是另一个摄像机。

1283
00:54:04.520 --> 00:54:07.280
And they call out the camera person's name, Mandy.
他们还喊出了摄像师的名字，曼迪。

1284
00:54:07.540 --> 00:54:07.880
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1285
00:54:08.160 --> 00:54:11.760
Mandy is their real B camera operator, Mandy Whitaker.
曼迪是他们真正的B机摄像师，曼迪·惠特克。

1286
00:54:12.080 --> 00:54:12.940
I thought so.
我也这么觉得。

1287
00:54:13.060 --> 00:54:16.240
I thought they were just looking right at their friend behind the camera.
我还以为他们只是在看着摄像机后面的朋友呢。

1288
00:54:16.680 --> 00:54:19.400
Mandy has also done camera operating on St. Dennis Medical,
曼迪还担任过《圣丹尼斯医疗》和

1289
00:54:19.620 --> 00:54:21.160
and it's always sunny in Philadelphia.
《费城永远阳光灿烂》的摄像师。

1290
00:54:21.620 --> 00:54:24.420
Well, Cindy sees the cameras, and she's like, whatever, fine.
好吧，辛迪看到摄像机后，态度就像是，随便吧，好吧。

1291
00:54:24.680 --> 00:54:25.680
I'll give it up.
我招了。

1292
00:54:26.300 --> 00:54:30.440
And I thought Mary did such a great job in this moment as Cindy,
我觉得玛丽在这一幕中饰演辛迪表现得太棒了，

1293
00:54:30.560 --> 00:54:31.740
and I want you guys to hear it.
我想让你们听听看。

1294
00:54:32.300 --> 00:54:32.920
All right.
好的。

1295
00:54:33.060 --> 00:54:33.460
Oh, no.
噢，不。

1296
00:54:33.980 --> 00:54:36.640
So, I actually hate this job.
说实话，我讨厌这份工作。

1297
00:54:36.900 --> 00:54:37.220
Oh.
噢。

1298
00:54:38.480 --> 00:54:41.720
I hate this stupid polo they make you pay for yourself.
我讨厌这件还要自己掏钱买的破Polo衫。

1299
00:54:42.840 --> 00:54:46.340
I was too scared to be a geologist, and now it's too late.
我以前太害怕而不敢当地理学家，现在已经太迟了。

1300
00:54:47.500 --> 00:54:48.980
So, get your notepads out.
所以，把你们的记事本拿出来。

1301
00:54:50.100 --> 00:54:51.220
Let's burn it all down.
把它全部烧毁吧。

1302
00:54:53.300 --> 00:54:55.340
Let's get some water, and then we can get into it.
我们先弄点水，然后就开始吧。

1303
00:54:55.460 --> 00:54:55.980
I'll help.
我来帮忙。

1304
00:54:56.020 --> 00:54:56.740
Why don't we get some water?
我们怎么不去弄点水呢？

1305
00:54:56.900 --> 00:54:57.860
I'm going to write it, too.
我也要把它写下来。

1306
00:54:58.000 --> 00:54:58.460
We're all good.
我们都很好。

1307
00:54:58.600 --> 00:54:59.040
I'll write it.
我来写。

1308
00:54:59.160 --> 00:54:59.360
Well.
好吧。

1309
00:55:01.370 --> 00:55:03.070
Let's burn it all down, lady.
把它全烧了吧，女士。

1310
00:55:03.070 --> 00:55:06.650
Cindy would make a great guest on Office Ladies Burn It to the Ground.
辛迪会成为《办公室女士》“烧毁它”节目的绝佳嘉宾。

1311
00:55:06.790 --> 00:55:07.870
That's what I thought.
我也是这么想的。

1312
00:55:09.510 --> 00:55:10.850
She's ready to talk.
她准备好谈谈了。

1313
00:55:11.350 --> 00:55:13.410
I mean, she's just so good.
我的意思是，她实在是太棒了。

1314
00:55:13.590 --> 00:55:14.870
I thought she was great.
我觉得她表现得很棒。

1315
00:55:15.330 --> 00:55:15.590
Yeah.
是啊。

1316
00:55:15.710 --> 00:55:19.590
She played it perfectly, and we were trading emails about it.
她演得太完美了，我们还为此交换了邮件。

1317
00:55:19.590 --> 00:55:26.890
And she said, Ang, I was reminded of a conversation we had at an Emmy party, and I was like, which
她说，安，我想起了我们在艾美奖派对上的一次对话，然后我就想，哪一个？

1318
00:55:26.890 --> 00:55:27.230
one?
一个？

1319
00:55:27.390 --> 00:55:31.230
And she said, so it was the night before party in 2024.
她说，那是2024年的展前派对。

1320
00:55:31.890 --> 00:55:35.890
She said, I was headed to film the paper that week, and you gave me some great advice.
她说，我那周正要去拍那张纸，你给了我很好的建议。

1321
00:55:36.230 --> 00:55:38.330
You said, quote, don't be the funny guy.
你说，原话是，别当那个搞笑的人。

1322
00:55:38.330 --> 00:55:41.450
And if you think you can make it even smaller, do.
如果你觉得还能再精简一点，那就去做。

1323
00:55:42.650 --> 00:55:46.210
Oh, you kind of gave her the direction that Ken Kuapis gave you.
哦，你有点像肯·库阿皮斯给你的指导那样去指导她。

1324
00:55:46.530 --> 00:55:46.930
Exactly.
完全正确。

1325
00:55:47.190 --> 00:55:50.510
And she said, so I just told the story, and I'm so glad I did.
她说，所以我只是讲了这个故事，我很高兴我这么做了。

1326
00:55:50.690 --> 00:55:52.210
She said, I thought it made me funnier.
她说，我觉得这让我更有趣了。

1327
00:55:52.450 --> 00:55:56.790
And she said, it's a really big set, and in my nervous actor brain, I could have absolutely
她说，这是一个非常大的布景，在我紧张的演员大脑里，我完全有可能用力过猛。

1328
00:55:56.790 --> 00:55:58.410
overshot and overplayed.
演过头了。

1329
00:55:58.470 --> 00:56:01.510
So I was really grateful for that insight from one who would know.
所以我非常感谢一个懂行的人提出的真知灼见。

1330
00:56:02.090 --> 00:56:06.950
Anyway, I didn't even remember saying that to her, but I'm so glad that it helped her.
总之，我甚至不记得对她说过这话，但我很高兴它帮到了她。

1331
00:56:07.010 --> 00:56:07.790
But she crushed it.
但她表现得太棒了。

1332
00:56:07.790 --> 00:56:08.690
She crushed it.
她太棒了。

1333
00:56:08.930 --> 00:56:09.470
She was great.
她表现得很好。

1334
00:56:09.990 --> 00:56:12.810
Well, listen, let's go back to this board meeting.
好吧，听着，让我们回到这个董事会会议上来。

1335
00:56:13.010 --> 00:56:14.070
They've been waiting for Ned.
他们一直在等内德。

1336
00:56:14.250 --> 00:56:15.610
They decide, forget it.
他们决定，算了吧。

1337
00:56:15.970 --> 00:56:17.890
We're just going to go on without him.
我们不等他了，直接开始吧。

1338
00:56:18.070 --> 00:56:19.290
What's on the docket today?
今天的议程是什么？

1339
00:56:20.190 --> 00:56:24.050
Well, what's on the docket is that they need money.
嗯，议程是他们需要资金。

1340
00:56:24.230 --> 00:56:25.270
They're over budget.
他们的预算超支了。

1341
00:56:25.670 --> 00:56:29.910
And Esmeralda says, listen, getting these original stories is expensive.
埃斯梅拉达说，听着，制作这些原创故事成本很高。

1342
00:56:29.910 --> 00:56:32.650
I think we need to go back to the way it was before Ned.
我认为我们需要回到内德之前的状态。

1343
00:56:33.350 --> 00:56:37.410
Yeah, basically, she's like, Ned's idea to do original stories was a bad idea.
是的，基本上，她觉得内德做原创故事的想法是个坏主意。

1344
00:56:37.410 --> 00:56:39.470
She's, again, trying to throw him under the bus.
她又想把责任推卸到他身上。

1345
00:56:39.630 --> 00:56:42.110
She says they should pay for the wire stories.
她说他们应该为电讯稿付钱。

1346
00:56:42.570 --> 00:56:48.990
But then Oscar brings up a line item that he found in the budget that's a little curious.
但随后奥斯卡提出了他在预算中发现的一个有点奇怪的项目。

1347
00:56:49.230 --> 00:56:55.670
It's a storage unit that they've been renting for nine years that's actually an apartment.
这是一个他们租了九年的储藏室，实际上是一套公寓。

1348
00:56:56.430 --> 00:57:00.770
Yeah, so in the Peacock version, you guys, it's extended.
是的，所以在孔雀版里，各位，这是加长版的。

1349
00:57:00.830 --> 00:57:07.730
And you sort of see Oscar really struggling because he knows Esmeralda and Ken are trying to sabotage Ned.
你能看出奥斯卡真的很纠结，因为他知道埃斯梅拉达和肯在试图破坏内德。

1350
00:57:07.910 --> 00:57:08.110
Yeah.
是的。

1351
00:57:08.110 --> 00:57:14.370
And you can also tell that Oscar maybe believes in Ned and thinks he should stick around and not get fired.
而且你也能看出来，奥斯卡可能挺信任内德的，觉得他应该留下来，别被解雇。

1352
00:57:14.550 --> 00:57:14.770
Yeah.
对。

1353
00:57:15.010 --> 00:57:18.310
So he decides to play this card to save the day.
所以他决定打出这张牌来解围。

1354
00:57:18.590 --> 00:57:18.730
Yeah.
对。

1355
00:57:18.770 --> 00:57:19.290
To save Ned.
为了救内德。

1356
00:57:19.610 --> 00:57:26.610
We find out that this storage unit, quote unquote, that's actually an apartment, is Ken's apartment.
我们发现这个所谓的“储物间”，其实是一套公寓，也就是肯的公寓。

1357
00:57:26.610 --> 00:57:34.550
He has a talking head where he says, yeah, Enervate rented him a small furnished apartment for a few weeks when he first moved over from the UK.
他有一段访谈镜头，里面说，对啊，当初他刚从英国搬过来时，恩内尔瓦特给他租了几周带家具的小公寓。

1358
00:57:35.550 --> 00:57:38.810
And somehow it got filed as a warehouse.
结果阴差阳错被归档成了仓库。

1359
00:57:39.110 --> 00:57:40.170
Ah, could you imagine?
啊，你能想象吗？

1360
00:57:40.710 --> 00:57:41.050
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1361
00:57:41.310 --> 00:57:48.490
So he's been sneaky sneak living rent-free and billing it back to the company as a storage facility.
所以他一直偷偷摸摸地免费白住，然后把这笔账当成仓储费用报销给公司。

1362
00:57:49.030 --> 00:57:51.730
So back in the meeting, Ken's like, you know what?
所以在后来的会议上，肯就说，你知道吗？

1363
00:57:51.970 --> 00:57:53.890
Let's get rid of this storage unit.
咱们把这个储物间取消吧。

1364
00:57:54.130 --> 00:57:56.010
No need to investigate what happened.
没必要去查到底发生了什么。

1365
00:57:56.330 --> 00:57:57.630
That's a waste of money.
那纯粹是浪费钱。

1366
00:57:57.890 --> 00:57:58.870
But look at that.
但你看看。

1367
00:57:58.870 --> 00:58:01.690
We'll have the money back in the budget and journalism wins.
这样预算里就能省下钱来，而且新闻业也赢了。

1368
00:58:02.150 --> 00:58:04.950
And then we have just some wrap-up moments, you know.
然后就到了一些收尾的时刻，你懂的。

1369
00:58:05.070 --> 00:58:09.310
So basically, Esmeralda knows that she's been beat once again.
所以基本上，埃斯梅拉达知道自己又一次输了。

1370
00:58:09.450 --> 00:58:12.030
And then we have this little moment with Nicole and Detrick.
然后我们看到了妮可和德特里克之间的这个小片段。

1371
00:58:12.390 --> 00:58:16.870
You know, he approaches her desk and he says, I figured out the lie.
你瞧，他走到她的办公桌前说，我猜到那个谎言是什么了。

1372
00:58:16.870 --> 00:58:18.630
It's that you dated a married guy.
就是你跟一个已婚男士谈过恋爱。

1373
00:58:18.810 --> 00:58:21.590
And she kind of goes, yeah, nailed it.
然后她差不多就是说，对啊，猜得真准。

1374
00:58:21.710 --> 00:58:29.430
And she just smiles to herself as he walks away because we realize that he's just there to protect her and help her save face.
等他走开时，她自己微微一笑，因为我们意识到他这么做只是为了保护她，帮她保住面子。

1375
00:58:29.430 --> 00:58:31.750
And she doesn't need to be embarrassed around him.
而且她在他面前也不用感到尴尬了。

1376
00:58:32.530 --> 00:58:32.730
Yeah.
对。

1377
00:58:32.990 --> 00:58:34.990
I mean, it was a very sweet gesture.
我的意思是，这真的是个很贴心的举动。

1378
00:58:35.430 --> 00:58:35.650
Yeah.
对。

1379
00:58:35.810 --> 00:58:39.270
I think he sort of could see that she was bummed.
我觉得他大概能看出她挺沮丧的。

1380
00:58:39.390 --> 00:58:40.710
She was kind of shutting down.
她有点快要自闭了。

1381
00:58:40.930 --> 00:58:41.290
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1382
00:58:41.290 --> 00:58:45.630
And so he went over and, like, gave her an out.
所以他就走过去，相当于给她找了个台阶下。

1383
00:58:46.230 --> 00:58:47.030
Yeah, exactly.
对，完全是这样。

1384
00:58:47.390 --> 00:58:53.890
And then we have this mare talking head where she's made the decision to stay, you know.
然后我们看到梅尔的访谈镜头，她已经决定留下来了。

1385
00:58:53.890 --> 00:58:56.410
She's not going to take the job at the hotel.
她不打算去酒店工作了。

1386
00:58:56.510 --> 00:59:00.490
She says, I'm young and the hospitality world will always be there.
她说，我还年轻，酒店业大门永远为我敞开。

1387
00:59:00.670 --> 00:59:00.910
Yeah.
对。

1388
00:59:01.290 --> 00:59:02.690
And then she says bye to Ned.
然后她跟内德告别。

1389
00:59:02.910 --> 00:59:04.330
She says, all right, I'll see you tomorrow.
她说，行吧，那明天见。

1390
00:59:04.370 --> 00:59:05.350
And he's like, you will?
结果他说，真的吗？

1391
00:59:05.490 --> 00:59:06.450
He's, like, so happy.
他看起来高兴坏了。

1392
00:59:06.630 --> 00:59:07.030
Yes.
没错。

1393
00:59:07.030 --> 00:59:09.490
And they do this very awkward fist bump.
然后他们碰了个极其尴尬的拳。

1394
00:59:09.510 --> 00:59:11.010
And he's like, all right, buddy.
接着他说，行啦，老兄。

1395
00:59:11.210 --> 00:59:12.610
And she's like, yeah, right, dude.
而她则说，行吧，随你，老哥。

1396
00:59:12.890 --> 00:59:16.290
And that's where we get the name of this episode, Buddy and the Dude.
这就是本集剧名《伙伴与老哥》的由来。

1397
00:59:16.510 --> 00:59:16.890
Yeah.
对。

1398
00:59:17.070 --> 00:59:19.150
And that's the end of this paper episode.
这一集的报社故事就到这里。

1399
00:59:19.730 --> 00:59:20.890
It's very sweet.
真的很温馨。

1400
00:59:21.150 --> 00:59:24.370
Mare and Ned finished their first article, and it's a big win.
梅尔和内德完成了他们的第一篇报道，这可真是一次大胜。

1401
00:59:24.690 --> 00:59:24.990
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1402
00:59:25.030 --> 00:59:26.570
I was very excited for them.
我为他们感到非常兴奋。

1403
00:59:26.990 --> 00:59:27.430
Yeah.
对。

1404
00:59:27.670 --> 00:59:34.590
And we're starting to see a little budding romance, maybe, or friendship, at least, between Detrick and Nicole.
而且我们开始看到德里克和妮可之间可能正在萌芽一段浪漫，或者至少是友谊。

1405
00:59:34.590 --> 00:59:42.110
And we're starting to see that Oscar might be invested in this idea of a successful paper.
而且我们开始发现奥斯卡可能很投入办一份成功报纸这个想法。

1406
00:59:42.330 --> 00:59:43.290
And there you have it.
事情就是这样。

1407
00:59:43.430 --> 00:59:44.270
There you have it.
就是这样。

1408
00:59:44.650 --> 00:59:51.310
Big thank yous to Greg Daniels, Creed Bratton, Chelsea Fry, and Patrick Kang.
非常感谢格雷格·丹尼尔斯、克里德·布拉顿、切尔西·弗莱和帕特里克·康。

1409
00:59:51.550 --> 00:59:54.370
Thank you guys so much for talking to us about this episode.
非常感谢你们跟我们聊这一集。

1410
00:59:54.690 --> 00:59:56.070
We're really enjoying this.
我们真的很享受。

1411
00:59:56.170 --> 00:59:57.350
I can't wait for next week.
我等不及下周了。

1412
00:59:57.530 --> 00:59:57.890
Yes.
是的。

1413
00:59:58.010 --> 01:00:02.550
And thank you to everyone that's gone to the website and to our little folders and written comments or questions.
也谢谢所有去网站和我们的文件夹留言或提问的每个人。

1414
01:00:02.750 --> 01:00:03.370
Keep them coming.
请继续保持。

1415
01:00:03.370 --> 01:00:04.830
We'll see you next week.
我们下周见。

1416
01:00:04.990 --> 01:00:05.450
See you then.
